# The Night Lord's second class node: one huge shuriken thrown forward, hitting
# everything it passes, then spinning where it stops.
#
# GMS's own figures: 285+11x% seven times on six enemies, on a 25s cooldown. The
# tooltip never gives the beat; the client's `subTime` is 180ms, the field Bolt
# Barrage and Inhuman Speed take theirs from. The shuriken lasts for its flight
# (600px at v25, about 0.4s) plus 2 seconds of spinning, so fourteen strikes
# land: 60,270% at max, or 2,411%/s over the cooldown, just under Bolt Barrage's
# 2,580%/s.
#
# `cast_interval_ms` fits for two reasons: it is GMS's own beat, and strikes
# landing one at a time is what a shuriken that keeps hitting whatever is left
# looks like in an engine without positions.
#
# The mark is the cost. GMS cuts Assassin's Mark to 40% of its normal chance on
# this swing, which would otherwise roll it fourteen times a press.
#
# Dropped: the recast that stops the shuriken in place, which needs a place, and
# immunity to attack reflection, which nothing here has.
name: "Shurrikane"
description:
  "Throws a massive shuriken said to be used by the thieves of old. Reduced "
  "chance of activating Assassin's Mark."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_NIGHT_LORD_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
final_attack_label: "Assassin's Mark"
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_CLAW
base_delay_ms: 480
cooldown_seconds: 25.0
max_enemies: 6
lines: 7
casts: 14
cast_interval_ms: 180
base {
  skill_pct: 2.96
  final_attack_chance_cut: 0.60
}
per_level { skill_pct: 0.11 }
